title: SPIR-V Specification
author: John Kessenich, Google
author: Boaz Ouriel, Intel
author: Raun Krisch, Intel
changes:

=== Changes from Version 1.6, Revision 2

- Reserve enumerants for:
 * SPV_KHR_ray_tracing_position_fetch
 * SPV_QCOM_image_processing
 * SPV_ARM_core_builtins
 * SPV_NV_shader_invocation_reorder
 * SPV_NV_displacement_micromap
 * SPV_AMDX_shader_enqueue
 * SPV_INTEL_fp_max_error
 * SPV_INTEL_kernel_attributes
 * SPV_INTEL_cache_controls
 * SPV_INTEL_global_variable_fpga_decorations
 * SPV_INTEL_global_variable_host_access
 * SPV_INTEL_bfloat16_conversion
 * SPV_INTEL_runtime_aligned
 * SPV_INTEL_fpga_argument_interfaces
 * SPV_INTEL_fpga_dsp_control
 * SPV_INTEL_fpga_invocation_pipelining_attributes
 * SPV_INTEL_fpga_latency_control
 * SPV_INTEL_fpga_loop_controls
 * SPV_INTEL_fpga_memory_attributes
 * SPV_EXT_image_raw10_raw12
 * SPV_EXT_shader_tile_image
 * SPV_EXT_mesh_shader
 * SPV_EXT_opacity_micromap

- Other changes from public headers
 * Added <<Source_Language, source languages>> HERO_C, NZSL, WGSL, and Slang
 * Removed the *Kernel* enabling capability from the <<Sampler_Addressing_Mode, sampler addressing modes>>.

- Fix SPIR-V Registry issues:
 * #72: Be consistent in <<OpTypeBool, *OpTypeBool*>> that SPIR-V can support Booleans in the *UniformConstant* storage class.
 * #197: Clarify that <<OpQuantizeToF16,*OpQuantizeToF16*>> must flush denormalized values to 0.

- Fix Khronos SPIR-V issues:
 * #689: Clarify use of *OpPhi* on *OpTypeImage* in the <<Validation, universal validation rules>>.
 * #708: Remove unused definitions of Break Block, Continue Block and Return Block.
 * #707: Clarify that using a bad _Direction_ in <<OpGroupNonUniformQuadSwap,*OpGroupNonUniformQuadSwap*>>
         is invalid SPIR-V.
 * #712: Clarify multiple *UserSemantic* <<Decoration, decorations>> can apply to a variable or structure member.
 * #731: Clarify that <<AliasingSection,aliasing>> is based on dynamic execution.
 * #736: Clarify that <<OpArrayLength,*OpArrayLength*>> may have a logical pointer operand in the <<Validation, universal validation rules>>.
 * #737: Clarify <<Validation,validation rule>> restricting <<OpConstantNull,*OpConstantNull*>> from pointing into
         the *PhysicalStorageBuffer* <<Storage_Class, storage class>>.
 * #738: Restrict <<OpImageQueryLevels, *OpImageQueryLevels*>> and <<OpImageQueryLod, *OpImageQueryLod*>> images to have MS of 0.
 * #295: Clarify that the *ZeroExtend* and *SignExtend* <<Image_Operands, image operands>> are not valid together.
 * #753: Clarify that *GroupNonUniformQuad* instructions are not affected by their execution scopes, and require the value to be
         <<Subgroup, subgroup>>.
 * #754: Modify _ClusterSize_ operands to refer to the size of the group of invocations participating in the instruction
         instead of always talking about *SubgroupSize*.
 * #755: Clarify set of invocations affected by a group operation:
   ** Add definition of group (invocations).
   ** Add definition of <<Workgroup, workgroup>>.
   ** Link to new definitions throughout the specification.
   ** Define sizes of <<Quad, quad>>, <<Subgroup, subgroup>>, and <<Workgroup, workgroup>>.
   ** Modify description of _Execution Scope_ to clarify that it identifies the group an instruction affects.
   ** Remove restrictions on _Execution Scope_ for most instructions, leaving it up to client APIs to restrict them.
   ** Clarify that <<Non-Uniform, non-uniform instructions>> require the value of _Execution Scope_ to be <<Subgroup, subgroup>>.
   ** Clarify that *GroupNonUniformQuad* instructions are not affected by their execution scopes.
 * #757: Restrict the type of ballot bit sets to be 4-component vectors of 32-bit unsigned integers in
         <<Non-Uniform,Non-Uniform Instructions>>.
 * #758: Add the definition of a <<Cluster, cluster>>.
 * #772: Clarify that <<OpPtrAccessChain,*OpPtrAccessChain*>> does not dereference any pointer.
 * #750: Update <<Validation,validation rules>> to reflect support for image and sampler array non-uniform indexing.

- Khronos SPIR-V MRs:
 * #261: Clarify that _Sampled_ operand for <<OpImageSparseFetch, *OpImageSparseFetch*>> is restricted to 1,
  bringing it in line with the constraint for <<OpImageFetch, *OpImageFetch*>>.
 * #280: <<OpControlBarrier, Control barriers>> wait only for active invocations.

- Deprecations:
 * Issue #756: Deprecated the use of <<BuiltIn, *BuiltIn*>> to decorate a constant to set its value
   and removed the deprecation of the *WorkgroupSize* <<BuiltIn, built-in>>.
   That is, *WorkgroupSize* is kept but no longer marked as deprecated (it is still required by OpenCL).
   The use of <<BuiltIn, *BuiltIn*>> to decorate a constant to set its value was only for *WorkgroupSize*,
   which has been superseded by the *LocalSizeId* <<Execution_Mode, execution mode>>.
 * MR #277: Deprecated *Simple* <<Memory_Model, memory model>> in favor of *GLSL450*.
